// M2 smoke test: pure-expression statements should compile to native
// opcodes (LoadConst / Add / Sub / Mul / Div / Lt / Eq / ...). Each
// statement here is a bare expression whose result is discarded — the
// IrCompiler is allowed to compile these natively without disturbing
// side effects.
//
// Run with --ir and RA_VM_STATS=1 to see the counters split.

print("=== M2 smoke ===");

// Bare expressions (no side effect). These should compile to native ops
// and run on the VM dispatch loop, not via OP_VISIT_AST.
5 + 3;
10 * 4;
20 / 5;
17 % 4;
1 == 1;
2 < 3;
4 > 5;
6 != 7;

// Mixed precedence — the IR compiler walks the binop tree.
((1 + 2) * 3 - 1) == 8;

// Each `var` declaration goes through OP_VISIT_AST (M2 does not compile
// declarations yet) but the subsequent bare expression compiles natively.
var a = 5;
var b = 10;
a + b;          // VariableAccess + Add at the VM level
a * b - 3;
a < b;

print("[M2] OK");
